                                CODING STYLE

COMMITS
    Commits should adhere to the following format:
        [module #12345] <Commit message>
    The module should refer to the name of the affected top-level module. Or, if
    it affects the whole project (think CMake changes, new dependencies, etc.),
    it should be "[project #12345]"

    The issue number is optional, and must be preceded by "I " if it is a
    private issue.

    Example commit names:
        GOOD: [binary_io] Fix something
        BAD:  [bit] Do something
        BAD:  [binio_interfaces] Add a thingamabob
               ^ Not a top-level module!
        BAD:  [bit]: Do something
                   ^ Shouldn't have a colon!
        GOOD: [binary_io #5] Fix something
                         ^ Refers to GitHub issue #5
        BAD:  [binary_io#12]
                        ^ Won't show up as a link in the GitHub web interface!
        GOOD: [binary_io I #1] Fix some issue
                           ^ Refers to Intra (private) issue #1
        BAD:  [binary_io I#3] Fix some other issue
                          ^ Won't show up as a link because of the missing space

